# Brotli-precompressed Unity WebGL assets - regenerated by
# scripts/compress-unity-data.cjs, not stored in git (500+ MB each).
# See docs/packaging.md.
artifacts/beach-volleyball/public/unity-build/Build/*.br

# Generated by mockupPreviewPlugin at dev-server start — regenerated on every
# run, so it only ever shows up as noise in git status.
artifacts/mockup-sandbox/src/.generated/

# SQLite sidecars — transient, recreated whenever the database is opened.
lib/db/*.sqlite-wal
lib/db/*.sqlite-shm
PR_BODY.md

# Replit's attached-assets drop box. The 1242 files already committed stay
# tracked - .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files - so the seed scripts in
# scripts/src keep resolving and clone size is unchanged. This only stops NEW
# pastes from being staged, which is where the 2.4 GB came from.
#
# Do NOT follow this with `git rm --cached attached_assets/`. That was
# considered and rejected. The scripts in scripts/src resolve these files
# through localImageUrl(), which on a miss logs a warning and returns null
# (scripts/src/lib/local-image.ts:27-29) instead of throwing. So on a fresh
# clone with the files untracked, a seed run would not fail - it would
# succeed while writing players and staff with no image, and the damage
# would only surface later as blank portraits in the UI. Seeding
# successfully-but-wrong is worse than not seeding at all, so the 1242
# files stay tracked.
#
# If anyone LFS-migrates this directory again and abandons it: the orphaned
# objects left in .git/lfs/objects can NEVER be reclaimed by `git lfs prune`,
# which protects locally-created, never-pushed objects even under --force.
# Delete them from the store by hand; do not waste time re-running prune.
attached_assets/
